<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  rev_reviewoutcome - the resolved, staff-facing outcome of a review round (rev_review.rev_outcome).

  DERIVED VALUE LIST - NOT SOURCED FROM THE TAD, AND NOT THE SAME KIND OF GAP AS
  rev_nonqualificationreason.xml'S PLACEHOLDER. The TAD names rev_outcome as a column
  ("rev_staffrecommendation, rev_outcome, rev_nonqualificationreason...") but gives it no type,
  no format and no value list - unlike rev_verdict1/rev_verdict2, which the same sentence gives
  "Approve . Defer . Reject" for explicitly, and unlike rev_nonqualificationreason, which the
  AMENDMENT block right after it gives three named values for (flagged there as a placeholder
  needing process-owner confirmation). This gap is different in kind: it is not an unconfirmed
  VALUE for a known shape, it is an UNSTATED shape. data-agent's own reasonable choice, flagged
  for reviewer confirmation rather than settled unilaterally:

    Approved / Deferred / Rejected mirror the three individual-trustee verdicts
    (rev_reviewverdict), because the Finalise Decisions flow (WBS 6.6, TAD section 5.7) has to
    resolve two trustee verdicts plus the process owner's own staff recommendation into ONE
    outcome that then drives whether a Grant row is created (FR-040, FR-047).

    Non-Qualifying is added as a fourth value because rev_nonqualificationreason exists as a
    companion column on the SAME table - an application can fail to qualify (score/age/
    location) without ever reaching a two-trustee verdict, and rev_outcome needs a value for
    that case too, or the Finalise Decisions flow has a case with a populated
    rev_nonqualificationreason and no rev_outcome to route on.

  Checked against rev_grantstatus and rev_applicationstatus before creating a new set (the
  task's own instruction): neither fits. rev_grantstatus describes what happens to an AWARDED
  grant AFTER a decision (Awarded -> Acceptance Issued -> ... -> Paid); rev_applicationstatus
  describes the application's OWN lifecycle across the whole case, most of which (Auto-pass,
  Under Review, Withdrawn, Incomplete, Grant Paid) has nothing to do with a panel round. Neither
  set has an "Approved/Deferred/Rejected/Non-Qualifying" shape.

  SHAPE: <Descriptions>/<displaynames> AFTER </options>, no per-option <Descriptions>, matching
  the ground-truthed rev_grantstatus.xml pattern exactly (IMP-0037).
-->
<optionset Name="rev_reviewoutcome" localizedName="Review Outcome">
  <OptionSetType>picklist</OptionSetType>
  <IsGlobal>1</IsGlobal>
  <IntroducedVersion>1.0.0.0</IntroducedVersion>
  <IsCustomizable>1</IsCustomizable>
  <options>
    <!-- 1 = Approved. The panel's resolved decision is to fund the application. -->
    <option value="1">
      <labels>
        <label description="Approved" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <!-- 2 = Deferred. The panel's resolved decision is to hold the application over to a
         later round rather than decide now. -->
    <option value="2">
      <labels>
        <label description="Deferred" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <!-- 3 = Rejected. The panel's resolved decision is not to fund the application. -->
    <option value="3">
      <labels>
        <label description="Rejected" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
    <!-- 4 = Non-Qualifying. The application never reached a two-trustee verdict at all -
         rev_nonqualificationreason records why. -->
    <option value="4">
      <labels>
        <label description="Non-Qualifying" languagecode="1033" />
      </labels>
    </option>
  </options>
  <Descriptions>
    <Description description="The resolved, staff-facing outcome of a review round, read by the Finalise Decisions flow (WBS 6.6, TAD section 5.7). DERIVED value list, flagged for reviewer confirmation - see this file's own header. Options are added over time but never renumbered or removed while rows reference them." languagecode="1033" />
  </Descriptions>
  <displaynames>
    <displayname description="Review Outcome" languagecode="1033" />
  </displaynames>
</optionset>
